relax and feel better. Whenever my muscles are\h
sore, this helps. Question. What's the difference\h\h

7
00:00:50,960 --> 00:01:01,680
between when and whenever? Whenever adds on the\h
additional meaning of frequency: it means every\h\h

8
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:11,520
time or anytime a certain event happens. In fact,\h
we can use every time to build the same adverb\h\h

9
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:20,240
clause. Take a look. Whenever my muscles are\h
sore, this helps. Every time my muscles are sore,\h\h

10
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:29,440
this helps. In everyday English, we can also\h
use anytime. Anytime my muscles are sore, this\h\h

11
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:38,720
helps. Remember that an adverb clause of time is\h
a dependent clause. It has a subject and a verb,\h\h

12
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:48,400
but it cannot stand alone as a complete sentence.\h
A dependent clause must join with a main clause,\h\h

13
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:56,560
an independent clause, and then together they\h
form a complex sentence. If that's too much\h\h

14
00:01:56,560 --> 00:02:02,320
grammar for your liking, just know that an\h
adverb clause needs to combine with a main\h\h

15
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:12,320
idea. Then you have a complete sentence. What\h
about when and while? How are they different?\h\h

16
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:20,560
Well, sometimes we can use either one to explain\h
that two things are happening at the same time.\h\h

17
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:26,960
People don't talk much when they're getting a\h
massage. People don't talk much while they're\h\h

18
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:37,920
getting a massage. In both sentences, the actions\h
happen at the same time. They're simultaneous.\h\h

19
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:47,600
We often use while with progressive forms, the\h
ing form, because the action is ongoing. However,\h\h

20
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:56,960
it's possible to use while with a simple form. For\h
example, I never listen to music while I work. Do\h\h

21
00:02:56,960 --> 00:03:06,800
you? You can answer yes, I listen to music while\h
I work. Or yes, I listen to music when I work.\h\h

22
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:14,880
They're basically the same, but remember that\h
when could be replaced by whenever to mean every\h\h

23
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:24,240
time or anytime. While emphasizes the ongoing\h
activities of listening and working. They're\h\h

24
